 to new ideas, show-off.\n\nGiven the criteria, reliability is crucial. B is very conscientious, which is strong reliability. D's reliability not explicitly mentioned. C's reliability not mentioned. A's reliability not mentioned. So B stands out for reliability.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well, C keeps calm, D responds adequately, A unknown. So B good.\n\nTechnical competence: B good at weather, computer; C understands complicated tech; D solves problems extremely well; A sees complex connections, spatial vision. Many.\n\nDecision quality: C can make correct decisions quickly; D solves problems extremely well; B not mentioned; A anticipates dangerous situations.\n\nCooperation: all have issues, but B makes nasty remarks, which is severe. C egocentric, difficulty communicating. D hot temper, know-it-all. A show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; A very good leadership; B not mentioned; C not mentioned.\n\nGiven the weight, reliability and stress are top. B is strongest there. Cooperation concerns can be mitigated with training. So I will recommend Candidate B.\n\nWe need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\". Provide evidence: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Also note the concern about nasty remarks but argue that strengths outweigh.\n\nLet's produce."}
